      "body": "When translating a compound assignment where an `int` variable is updated with a floating-point constant, c2go generates invalid Go code:\n```go\nb -= int32(3.5)\n```\nHowever, Go does not allow converting a non-integer floating-point constant such as `3.5` directly to `int32`, so the generated program fails to compile.\n**To Reproduce**\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int b = 20;\n    b -= 3.5;\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", b);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\nThe generated Go code contains:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n        var b int32 = int32(20)\n        b -= int32(3.5)\n        noarch.Printf((&[]byte(\"%d\\n\\x00\")[0]), b)\n        return\n}\n```\n**Observed Behavior**\n```\n# command-line-arguments\n./test.go:166:13: cannot convert 3.5 (untyped float constant) to type int32\n```\nThe invalid generated code is:\n```go\nb -= int32(3.5)\n```",
